<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38819" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπηλ-ῠς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠδος</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἔπηλυ, τό,
			</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπήλυθον</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who comes to</i> a place,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλθετ᾽ ἐπήλυδες αὖθις</span>
			<i>come</i> back <i>to me</i> (for they were going away), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1190
			</span></i> (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>incomer, stranger, foreigner,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτόχθων,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.78
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.197
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρας πολεμίους ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					243
				</span></i>
			 (troch.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				195
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.29
			</span></i>; Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. γένεσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Mx.</u>
					237b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					8.12.2
				</span></i>
			: also in neut. pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπήλυδα ἔθνεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.73
				</span></i>
			: neut. sg., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπήλυδος γένους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					1.60
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ ἔπηλυ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paus.
					2.5.3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
